---
description: When ticket work is finished, report merge and update status, then ask about open steps
alwaysApply: true
---

When the work for a ticket is finished, or the user asks whether a ticket is done, merged, or updated, check the closeout before the reply ends. This includes `/ticket NB-xx` after the acceptance work, a later pass that changes that ticket, and a question about a ticket that is already finished.

Check each item. Say in the reply which ones are still open. Name local, Linear, or both.

- **Local.** The ticket file still has an open acceptance box for work that was verified, or `status` is not `Done` after that work.
- **Linear.** The local description or status was not sent after the last edit. Description uses `node scripts/linear-sync.mjs push-one <id>`. Status uses `node scripts/linear-sync.mjs set-status <id> Done --push`.
- **Commit.** The ticket branch has uncommitted work for this ticket.
- **Push.** The ticket branch is ahead of its remote, or has no upstream.
- **Merge.** A Phase 2 ticket (`parent: NB-E6`) is not on `phase-2`. Merge that branch into `phase-2` only. Any other ticket is not on `main`.

Always end that reply with these two lines, even when both are already done. Do not hide a finished merge or a finished update inside one sentence that leaves those words out.

- **Updated.** Local: `Done` or not, and whether every verified acceptance box is checked. Linear: whether the description and the status were sent after the last edit. Name local, Linear, or both.
- **Merged.** A Phase 2 ticket (`parent: NB-E6`) is on `phase-2` or not, and whether `origin/phase-2` has that commit. Any other ticket is on `main` or not. Name the branch.

If every item is done, say that, then still write the Updated and Merged lines. Do not ask.

If any item is open, use AskQuestion before doing those steps. `allow_multiple` is true. Offer only the open steps, in this order, plus the two choices below. Put "Do the remaining steps" first.

- Do the remaining steps
- Update the local ticket
- Update Linear
- Commit
- Push
- Merge into phase-2
- Merge into main
- Leave it as it is

"Merge into phase-2" is only for a Phase 2 ticket. "Merge into main" is only for a ticket whose parent is not `NB-E6`. Do not offer a merge that the phase-2 rule forbids.

Wait for the selection. Then do the chosen steps in the order above. "Do the remaining steps" means every open step. "Leave it as it is" means change nothing else.
